From 000000000000000000000000000000000000000105 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: f <f@f>
Date: Sun, 23 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: Fix encoder profile and level when fw caps are zero

The vpu20_4v firmware of SM8450/SM8475 reports the encoder PROFILE and
LEVEL capabilities as 0, so the values userspace sets (H.264 baseline,
level 1.0) are passed through untranslated and the firmware dies at
session start. Fall back to the vendor table defaults for H.264: High
profile (HFI enum 4) and level 5.0 (HFI enum 14), matching
instance_data_waipio[] of the msm_vidc driver.

Encoder-only; the decoder keeps the firmware-reported values.

Local Diting bring-up change, not submitted upstream.
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
index 919a167..4029eda 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
@@ -416,6 +416,10 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen2_set_profile(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 plane)
 		break;
 	}
 
+	/* vpu20_4v: encoder PROFILE cap stays 0; use the vendor default */
+	if (inst->domain == ENCODER && !profile && inst->codec == V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264)
+		profile = 4; /* HFI AVC High profile */
+
 	inst_hfi_gen2->src_subcr_params.profile = profile;
 
 	return iris_hfi_gen2_session_set_property(inst,
@@ -448,6 +452,10 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen2_set_level(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 plane)
 		break;
 	}
 
+	/* vpu20_4v: encoder LEVEL cap stays 0; use the vendor default */
+	if (inst->domain == ENCODER && !level && inst->codec == V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264)
+		level = 14; /* HFI AVC level 5.0 */
+
 	inst_hfi_gen2->src_subcr_params.level = level;
 
 	return iris_hfi_gen2_session_set_property(inst,
